window.MONSTER_CHUNK_79 = [{"name":"Svathurim","cr":11,"xp":12800,"alignment":"CE","size":"Huge","type":"monstrous humanoid","subtypes":["cold"],"init":3,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":26,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":23,"ac_mods":"+4 armor, +3 Dex, +10 natural, +1 shield, -2 size","hp":147,"hd":"14d10+70","hdvalue":14,"fort":11,"ref":12,"will":11,"immunities":["cold"],"weaknesses":["vulnerable to fire"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50}],"melee":"mwk lance +22 (2d6+9/x3), gore +16 (2d6+4), 2 hooves +16 (1d8+4) or   2 slams +21 (1d8+9), gore +21 (2d6+9), 2 hooves +16 (1d8+4)","ranged":"mwk composite longbow +16 (2d6+9/x3)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (20 ft. with lance)","special_attacks":[{"type":"thunderous trample"},{"type":"trample","details":"1d8+13, DC 26"}],"strength":29,"dexterity":17,"constitution":20,"intelligence":10,"wisdom":14,"charisma":11,"baseatk":14,"cmb":25,"cmb_special":"+2 vs. bull rush, +2 vs. overrun","cmd":38,"cmd_special":"+2 vs. bull rush, +2 vs. overrun, +12 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Charge Through"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Overrun"},{"feat":"Intimidating Prowess"},{"feat":"Natural Jouster"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":12,"special":"+20 when jumping"},{"skill":"Climb","value":12},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":25},{"skill":"Perception","value":19},{"skill":"Survival","value":14},{"skill":"Swim","value":20}],"languages":["Giant","Skald"],"sq":[{"type":"skyrunner"},{"type":"undersized weapons"}],"environments":["cold hills","any mountains","any plains"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","warband (3-6)","clan (1-4 svathurim plus 2-12 frost giants)"],"treasure":"standard (mwk chain shirt, mwk light steel shield, mwk lance, mwk composite longbow with 40 arrows)","description_visual":"This hulking creature has the lower body of a massive stallion with eight thick legs. Rising from its equine body is the trunk of a muscled humanoid with icy blue skin and a prodigious white beard rimed with ice. Piercing blue eyes glare beneath beetled brows and a spiraling pair of horns which curl upward.","source":"AP 69","special_abilities":[{"type":"Skyrunner","kind":"Su","details":"When charging, running, or taking a double move, a svathurim can stride across open air as if it were using air walk. This movement is very taxing, and a svathurim must succeed at a DC 14 Constitution check at the end of each round it uses this ability to avoid being fatigued for 1 minute. This DC increases by 2 each round after the first. Returning to the ground resets the DC to 14, but doesn't negate any ongoing fatigue or exhaustion. A svathurim cannot trample when using this ability."},{"type":"Thunderous Trample","kind":"Su","details":"Any creature damaged by a svathurim's trample attack must succeed at a DC 22 Fortitude save or be deafened for 1 minute. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Undersized Weapons","kind":"Ex","details":"Although a svathurim is Huge, its upper torso is the same size as that of a Large humanoid. As a result, it wields weapons as if they were one size category smaller than their actual size (Large for most svathurim)."}],"description":"Ancient tales claim the first svathurims spawned from Thremyr, akin to the creation stories of frost giants, ice trolls, winter wolves, and other creatures of snow and ice. The stories claim that when Thremyr fell into the Steaming Sea, he shed great icebergs that transformed into smaller copies of the god himself. The frost giants, spawned from his shedding body, worship this slumbering god as their creator, and thus consider svathurims their kin. The hindquarters of an adult svathurim are up to 10 ft. tall and 16 ft. long, while their giant trunk and head reach up to 18 ft. on average. Svathurims typically weigh over 5 tons and may live up to 500 years, far longer than their frost giant kin.\n\nEcology\n\nSvathurims dwell deep in the frozen wastes of the tundra and arctic regions of Golarion, amid the great glaciers covering the Crown of the World. They occasionally travel along the frozen shores of polar seas, hunting seals, walruses, and whales that venture too close to shore or dragging vast nets through subarctic shallows during salmon runs. It is uncommon for svathurims to live in the vast boreal forests of the north, where their great bulk impedes movement among the trees, though some clans do dwell in the high mountains, springing from peak to peak in prodigious leaps and using their supernatural skyborne gallops.\n\nSvathurims are omnivorous and always hungry, able to subsist on scrub plants and kelp in times of great need, or even to eke out bare subsistence on the algae and lichen embedded in ice and rocks. However, they greatly prefer fresh, uncooked meat, and will devour every scrap of whatever they kill. Their grinding teeth are capable of reducing bone to meal, so even the toughest of a victim's remains generally end up in a svathurim's gullet. In the cold and pitiless environment of the north, nothing can be wasted.\n\nSvathurim males outnumber females by a wide margin, and these creatures are indiscriminate in their mating habits. The rare svathurim mares are little more selective in their affections than the males, and there is no shortage of males willing to court them. Ironically, many adult male svathurim are killed or wounded in competition for the attentions of females, either maimed and driven off by more dominant males or slain and presented as a trophy to prove worthiness to a female. Female svathurim are never monogamous, though, as mating with many males confuses the issue of parentage enough to keep their offspring safe from the predations of many adult males, lest a male inadvertently eradicate a foal svathurim that may be his own flesh and blood.\n\nHabitat & Society\n\nSvathurims live in clans, typically headed by the strongest and most accomplished hunter in the group, whether male or female. In some clans, svathurims gain status by the number of offspring they produce, though parentage is diff icult to prove for males and leads to frequent disputes.\n\nWhere females are both strong and fertile, they are able to assert dominance both by their own strength and by the loyalty and support of those children willing to fight for them. Of course, no svathurim can feel too secure in his position, as once-loyal supporters may shift their allegiance on a whim, and even faithful children may decide that they have grown strong enough to betray their parent to a rival or gather support (often from siblings) to take power in their own right.\n\nSvathurims sometimes build large corrals of stone, ice, or rarely bone or wood where such materials are available in plenty. Usually unroofed, these monolithic barriers serve mostly to keep predators away from their young or to protect their stores of treasure or food gathered by the clan from raiders. A rare few svathurims build more secure enclosed lodges or delve permanent hostels in caves. Svathurims that choose to settle in one area are most likely to live among frost giants.\n\nFrost giants view svathurims with a mix of fear, respect, awe, and revulsion. Most know well the tale of the svathurims' creation, and while not all take this as evidence of pseudo-divinity and a shared creation myth, few deny the svathurims' speed, strength, and skill at hunting and killing. For some giant clans, satisfying a svathurim's whims is a small price to pay for the advantages gained by an alliance with them Svathurims collect treasure as frost giants do, favoring precious metals in raw nuggets that are then hammered into crude tribal jewelry. Bracelets, armlets, and rings and chains they can braid into their hair, beards, and long horse-like tails are favored treasures, as are inlays and carvings made of mammoth or walrus ivory. Those in subarctic regions collect amber and rare boreal hardwoods, polishing the latter to a luxurious shine and engraving them with runic inscriptions and genealogies both real and imagined.","ecology":"Svathurims dwell deep in the frozen wastes of the tundra and arctic regions of Golarion, amid the great glaciers covering the Crown of the World. They occasionally travel along the frozen shores of polar seas, hunting seals, walruses, and whales that venture too close to shore or dragging vast nets through subarctic shallows during salmon runs. It is uncommon for svathurims to live in the vast boreal forests of the north, where their great bulk impedes movement among the trees, though some clans do dwell in the high mountains, springing from peak to peak in prodigious leaps and using their supernatural skyborne gallops.\n\nSvathurims are omnivorous and always hungry, able to subsist on scrub plants and kelp in times of great need, or even to eke out bare subsistence on the algae and lichen embedded in ice and rocks. However, they greatly prefer fresh, uncooked meat, and will devour every scrap of whatever they kill. Their grinding teeth are capable of reducing bone to meal, so even the toughest of a victim's remains generally end up in a svathurim's gullet. In the cold and pitiless environment of the north, nothing can be wasted.\n\nSvathurim males outnumber females by a wide margin, and these creatures are indiscriminate in their mating habits. The rare svathurim mares are little more selective in their affections than the males, and there is no shortage of males willing to court them. Ironically, many adult male svathurim are killed or wounded in competition for the attentions of females, either maimed and driven off by more dominant males or slain and presented as a trophy to prove worthiness to a female. Female svathurim are never monogamous, though, as mating with many males confuses the issue of parentage enough to keep their offspring safe from the predations of many adult males, lest a male inadvertently eradicate a foal svathurim that may be his own flesh and blood.","habitat_society":"Svathurims live in clans, typically headed by the strongest and most accomplished hunter in the group, whether male or female. In some clans, svathurims gain status by the number of offspring they produce, though parentage is diff icult to prove for males and leads to frequent disputes.\n\nWhere females are both strong and fertile, they are able to assert dominance both by their own strength and by the loyalty and support of those children willing to fight for them. Of course, no svathurim can feel too secure in his position, as once-loyal supporters may shift their allegiance on a whim, and even faithful children may decide that they have grown strong enough to betray their parent to a rival or gather support (often from siblings) to take power in their own right.\n\nSvathurims sometimes build large corrals of stone, ice, or rarely bone or wood where such materials are available in plenty. Usually unroofed, these monolithic barriers serve mostly to keep predators away from their young or to protect their stores of treasure or food gathered by the clan from raiders. A rare few svathurims build more secure enclosed lodges or delve permanent hostels in caves. Svathurims that choose to settle in one area are most likely to live among frost giants.\n\nFrost giants view svathurims with a mix of fear, respect, awe, and revulsion. Most know well the tale of the svathurims' creation, and while not all take this as evidence of pseudo-divinity and a shared creation myth, few deny the svathurims' speed, strength, and skill at hunting and killing. For some giant clans, satisfying a svathurim's whims is a small price to pay for the advantages gained by an alliance with them Svathurims collect treasure as frost giants do, favoring precious metals in raw nuggets that are then hammered into crude tribal jewelry. Bracelets, armlets, and rings and chains they can braid into their hair, beards, and long horse-like tails are favored treasures, as are inlays and carvings made of mammoth or walrus ivory. Those in subarctic regions collect amber and rare boreal hardwoods, polishing the latter to a luxurious shine and engraving them with runic inscriptions and genealogies both real and imagined."},{"name":"Svathurim","cr":11,"xp":12800,"alignment":"CE","size":"Huge","type":"monstrous humanoid","subtypes":["cold"],"init":3,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":26,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":23,"ac_mods":"+4 armor, +3 Dex, +10 natural, +1 shield, -2 size","hp":147,"hd":"14d10+70","hdvalue":14,"fort":11,"ref":12,"will":11,"immunities":["cold"],"weaknesses":["vulnerable to fire"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50}],"melee":"mwk lance +22 (3d6+13/x3), gore +21 (2d6+9), 2 hooves +16 (1d8+4)","ranged":"mwk composite longbow +16 (3d6+9/x3)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (20 ft. with lance)","special_attacks":[{"type":"natural jouster"},{"type":"thunderous trample"},{"type":"trample","details":"1d8+13, DC 26"}],"strength":29,"dexterity":17,"constitution":20,"intelligence":10,"wisdom":14,"charisma":11,"baseatk":14,"cmb":25,"cmb_special":"+2 vs. bull rush, +4 vs. overrun","cmd":38,"cmd_special":"+2 vs. bull rush, +2 vs. overrun, +12 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Charge Through"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Greater Overrun"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Overrun"},{"feat":"Intimidating Prowess"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":12,"special":"+20 when jumping"},{"skill":"Climb","value":12},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":25},{"skill":"Perception","value":19},{"skill":"Survival","value":14},{"skill":"Swim","value":20}],"languages":["Common","Giant"],"sq":[{"type":"skyrunner"},{"type":"undersized weapons"}],"environments":["cold hills","any mountains","any plains"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","war band (3-6)","clan (1-4 svathurim plus 2-12 frost giants)"],"treasure":"standard (mwk chain shirt, mwk light steel shield, mwk composite longbow with 40 arrows, mwk lance)","description_visual":"This hulking creature has the lower half of an eight-legged stallion and the upper half of a horned frost giant.","source":"Monster Codex","special_abilities":[{"type":"Natural Jouster","kind":"Ex","details":"A svathurim can wield a lance one-handed as if it were mounted, and it deals double damage with a lance while charging."},{"type":"Skyrunner","kind":"Su","details":"When charging, running, or taking a double move, a svathurim can stride across open air as if it were using air walk. This movement is very taxing; a svathurim must succeed at a DC 14 Constitution check at the end of each round it uses this ability or become fatigued for 1 minute. This DC increases by 2 for each round after the first. Returning to the ground resets the DC to 14, but doesn't negate any ongoing fatigue or exhaustion. A svathurim cannot trample when using this ability."},{"type":"Thunderous Trample","kind":"Su","details":"Any creature damaged by a svathurim's trample attack must succeed at a DC 22 Fortitude save or be deafened for 1 minute. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"Svathurims and frost giants consider each other allies and distant kin. The hindquarters of an adult svathurim are up to 10 ft. tall and 16 ft. long, while its giant trunk and head reach up to 18 ft. in height. They typically weigh more than 5 tons and may live up to 500 years. Svathurims dwell in arctic regions, galloping along the shores of polar seas or between high mountain peaks, with individuals organized into clans headed by the strongest hunters.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Taotieh","cr":11,"xp":12800,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"construct","init":2,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":28,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":26,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +17 natural, -1 size","hp":107,"hd":"14d10+30","hdvalue":14,"fort":4,"ref":6,"will":15,"dr":"10/adamantine","immunities":["construct traits"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"electricity","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"weaknesses":["vulnerable to sonic"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"bite +23 (1d8+10 plus grab), 2 claws +23 (1d6+10 plus grab)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"pounce"},{"type":"rake","details":"2 claws +23, 1d6+10"},{"type":"swallow whole","details":"suffocation, AC 18, hardness 8, 25 hp"}],"strength":30,"dexterity":15,"wisdom":14,"charisma":1,"baseatk":14,"cmb":29,"cmd":41,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","pair"],"treasure":"incidental","description_visual":"This white marble statue resembles a large feline, but its body and face are covered in decorative etchings and runes.","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 3","special_abilities":[{"type":"Swallow Whole","kind":"Su","details":"A taotieh can expand its jaws to swallow Large or smaller creatures. When swallowed, a victim is transported to its own lightless pocket dimension-a stone prison just large enough to contain the victim. Creatures don't take damage within this pocket dimension, but there is only enough air inside to last for 3 rounds. At the end of the third round, the trapped creature must hold its breath or risk suffocation. A creature that attempts to carve its way out of this dimension with a weapon must be able to penetrate the surrounding walls' hardness 8. When a creature manages to cut its way out of this dimension, it appears to leap out of the taotieh's mouth to emerge into any square adjacent to the taotieh's space-no actual hole is created in the creature, and new creatures that are swallowed later must cut their own way out. When a taotieh is destroyed, its body bursts open to allow the contents of its extradimensional stomachs to spill out into adjacent spaces. A taotieh can swallow up to four creatures at any one time."}],"description":"Symbols of power but also of gluttony, taotiehs are guardian constructs formed of stone and built around a pocket of extradimensional space. Taotiehs are used to ward sacred or secluded areas from enemies and trespassers. Their semblance to tigers extends even to the animal's abilities in combat, as taotiehs are feared for their vicious attacks. The extradimensional space at the core of a taotieh allows the construct to swallow opponents of its own size and then shunt its victims into an airless pocket of space inside. A creature capable of existing without air could well spend an eternity inside a taotieh if it couldn't smash its way out or escape via plane-traversing magic, in which case it must wait for outside forces to slay its captor. Tales abound of great treasures and even greater dangers being unleashed upon a taotieh's destruction.\n\nConstruction\n\nA taotieh is built from 12,000 pounds of marble, treated with special unguents and chemicals worth 5,000 gp.\n\nTAOTIEH\n\nCL 14th; Price 105,000 gp\n\nConstruction\n\nRequirements Craft Construct, geas/quest, limited wish, plane shift, creator must be caster level 14th; Skill Craft (sculpture) or Craft (stonemasonry) DC 25; Cost 55,000 gp","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Tetrolimulus","cr":11,"xp":12800,"alignment":"NE","size":"Large","type":"magical beast","subtypes":["aquatic"],"init":8,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":27,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":23,"ac_mods":"+4 Dex, +14 natural, -1 size","hp":147,"hd":"14d10+70","hdvalue":14,"fort":16,"ref":13,"will":8,"resists":[{"type":"cold","value":10}],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50},{"type":"swim","speed":50}],"melee":"2 claws +19 (2d6+6/x4), sting +17 (1d6+3 plus poison)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"poison"},{"type":"pounce"}],"strength":22,"dexterity":18,"constitution":21,"intelligence":3,"wisdom":12,"charisma":9,"baseatk":14,"cmb":25,"cmb_special":"+2 vs. overrun, +2 vs. sunder","cmd":39,"cmd_special":"+2 vs. overrun, +2 vs. sunder, +4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Endurance"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lunge"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Run"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":10},{"skill":"Perception","value":7},{"skill":"Survival","value":14}],"sq":[{"type":"amphibious"},{"type":"shoreline mastery"}],"environments":["temperate coasts"],"organizations":["solitary","pair"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"From a body like a strange crab sprouts the torso of a praying mantis, clad in coral-colored crustacean armor. Swaying hypnotically, it rattles razor-sharp claws and raises its long, rapier-like tail stinger.","source":"AP 58","special_abilities":[{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Tetrodotoxin: Sting-injury; save Fort DC 22; frequency once; initial effect staggered for 1 round, secondary effect paralysis for 1d4 rounds; cure 2 consecutive saves."},{"type":"Shoreline Mastery","kind":"Ex","details":"The multi-limbed nature of the crab half of the tetrolimulus allows it to ignore the effects of uneven or difficult terrain. This doesn't apply to terrain magically manipulated to impede movement."}],"description":"A terrifying mix of prehistoric arthropod and heavily armored mantis, the tetrolimulus is the stuff of nightmares for shipwrecked and abandoned mariners. Plated with a spiny crustacean exoskeleton, the upper body of the tetrolimulus is reminiscent of a very robust kind of mantis. Its raptorial forelimbs, folded as if in prayer, flash forward with frightening speed and precision to brutally slice opponents before they have had a chance to act. Captains and mutineers alike are quick to remind their enemies of these deadly claws and the creature's other name, the \"beach guillotine,\" for the brutal justice it exacts on those put ashore for choosing the wrong side in a mutiny.\n\nWith somewhat less panache, the tetrolimulus is often described as the \"sea-mantis\" because it resembles a crab's strong legs and shell merged with a mantis' powerful arms. Trailing behind is a scorpion's deadly stinger. The creature's durable, spiked shell covers five pairs of blade-like legs that work together to produce remarkable speeds even through challenging terrain. Truly a master of the beaches, the tetrolimulus has caught many mariners off guard with a blazing charge over varied terrain, perforating a noiseless trail through wet sand, then clattering over rocks with the sound of dice thrown across a table.\n\nIts final and most dangerous terror, held upright and waved like a regal scepter in combat, is the tetrolimulus's tail stinger. The stinger is razor sharp along its outer edge, but its neat incisions are nowhere near as dangerous as the poison that coats its blade. Those who succumb to a dose of poison-called tetrodotoxin-are soon to be a meal for the sea-mantis. Muscle spasms and cramps accompany a gradual slowing of movement, hinting at oncoming paralysis and the agony of a neat butchering while still alive for easy consumption. One of nature's cruelest poisons, tetrodotoxin is a popular tool of the Red Mantis assassins, who appreciate both the poison's painful efficacy and the mantis-form of its progenitor.\n\nEcology\n\nOut of the water, the tetrolimulus adopts an unusual swaying movement of the upper body. Although its purpose isn't entirely clear, it is thought that, much like the land-dwelling mantis, the movement enhances the creature's primitive vision and makes picking out prey by its own relative movement easier. It has been suggested that remaining completely still when confronted by a tetrolimulus may prevent detection, but none have been able to confirm the success of this tactic, and there are none who are confident enough of the theory to test it in the field.\n\nFemale tetrolimuluses, the hunters of the species, are by far the more aggressive. Rarely seen, males live in deeper waters as bottom feeders, emerging only in the mating season in early spring. At this time for a few days each year, both sexes make great journeys, sometimes of hundreds of miles, to return to ancient coastal breeding grounds. Here dominant and aggressive females meet and mate with the strongest of the smaller and more delicate males. Only a small number of these males get a chance to breed, and an even smaller number survive to return to the oceans. The energy and effort of their travels exhaust the females, and once they've been impregnated, the easiest and closest source of food is the weaker males surrounding them. A fertilized female may even continue to exhibit signs of availability to encourage more males to approach her—not for reproduction, but to satisfy her more immediate hunger.\n\nYoung are born at sea, and perhaps as payment for their strength and power later in life, they spend their first few months at the bottom of the food chain. Without the thick shells of maturity, they are easy prey, which contributes a great deal to population control of their species. As their shells thicken and harden, they start to enjoy a less harried existence, and by 6 months old they start to fight back. They reach maturity in 12 to 18 months and can live for up to 50 years.\n\nTetrolimuluses' behavior is largely instinct-driven, but during the breeding season the normally nomadic creatures will fight viciously to protect the shores of their ancestral breeding grounds. Even male sea-mantises rise to combat, though at sea they more commonly flee than risk confrontation.\n\nFemales can be found in the area of the Abendego Gulf, from Mediogalti Island all the way into the Shackles and as far north as the Sodden Lands. Even Rahadoum has seen the occasional tetrolimulus washed ashore to the south, where the creatures are feared as the twisted manifestations of Achaekek, conjured for worship by the Red Mantis and a stark reminder of the folly of religious devotion. There are descriptions of creatures similar to the tetrolimulus to the north, even into the Inner Sea, but these stories are as old and leaky as the ships of the pirates and traders who tell them and no reports of tetrolimuluses along the cost of Cheliax, for example, are younger than two generations.\n\nMuch of tetrolimuluses' bulk is armor, and despite their size they can survive on relatively small quantities of food. In perhaps the only mark of intelligence in their species, they try to avoid overfishing, instead roaming over several miles of coastline to balance their Ecology. The majority of their diet is fish and cephalopods, but they are competent trackers and follow hints of habitation on their beaches to devour any coast-dwelling mammals foolish enough to find themselves on the beaches, including humanoids. Like most animals, tetrolimuluses tend to avoid large settlements or areas frequently visited by humans. Remote or inaccessible beaches are the females' preferred habitat, but occasionally a powerful storm rolling out of the Eye of Abendego can toss them on more popular or even populous coastlines. Surprisingly high concentrations of the creatures are found around Mediogalti Island and its outlying cluster. Some suggest this is due to deliberate cultivation by the Red Mantis, thanks to the tetrolimulus's favorable form, but it may simply be because the treacherous waters and hidden coves are perfect for their reclusive lifestyle, and the frequent mutinies, shipwrecks, and foolish adventurers provide a varied and ample diet for the brutal predators.\n\nTetrodotoxin\n\nWhile none are stupid enough to actively farm sea-mantises, occasionally the corpse of one is washed up into the more accessible bays on the coasts of the Shackles or Mediogalti Island. Some of the more enterprising residents of Ilizmagorti have developed a method of harvesting the cruel tetrodotoxin poison, from which the tetrolimulus gets its name, for sale to the assassins of the Red Mantis.\n\nA single dose of tetrodotoxin sells for 1,300 gp. Its rarity and potency make it a valuable product, and prices outside the Shackles or Mediogalti Island can be 50-100% higher.\n\nOne dose of poison can be harvested from the corpse of a tetrolimulus, provided the lower half of the creature is intact. This requires a DC 25 Survival check, and even those who usually find themselves competent at skinning or gutting creatures struggle with the intricacies of the sharp tail stinger. In harvesting the tetrodotoxin poison, those without the poison use ability are subject to the standard 5% chance of self-poisoning.","ecology":"Out of the water, the tetrolimulus adopts an unusual swaying movement of the upper body. Although its purpose isn't entirely clear, it is thought that, much like the land-dwelling mantis, the movement enhances the creature's primitive vision and makes picking out prey by its own relative movement easier. It has been suggested that remaining completely still when confronted by a tetrolimulus may prevent detection, but none have been able to confirm the success of this tactic, and there are none who are confident enough of the theory to test it in the field.\n\nFemale tetrolimuluses, the hunters of the species, are by far the more aggressive. Rarely seen, males live in deeper waters as bottom feeders, emerging only in the mating season in early spring. At this time for a few days each year, both sexes make great journeys, sometimes of hundreds of miles, to return to ancient coastal breeding grounds. Here dominant and aggressive females meet and mate with the strongest of the smaller and more delicate males. Only a small number of these males get a chance to breed, and an even smaller number survive to return to the oceans. The energy and effort of their travels exhaust the females, and once they've been impregnated, the easiest and closest source of food is the weaker males surrounding them. A fertilized female may even continue to exhibit signs of availability to encourage more males to approach her—not for reproduction, but to satisfy her more immediate hunger.\n\nYoung are born at sea, and perhaps as payment for their strength and power later in life, they spend their first few months at the bottom of the food chain. Without the thick shells of maturity, they are easy prey, which contributes a great deal to population control of their species. As their shells thicken and harden, they start to enjoy a less harried existence, and by 6 months old they start to fight back. They reach maturity in 12 to 18 months and can live for up to 50 years.\n\nTetrolimuluses' behavior is largely instinct-driven, but during the breeding season the normally nomadic creatures will fight viciously to protect the shores of their ancestral breeding grounds. Even male sea-mantises rise to combat, though at sea they more commonly flee than risk confrontation.\n\nFemales can be found in the area of the Abendego Gulf, from Mediogalti Island all the way into the Shackles and as far north as the Sodden Lands. Even Rahadoum has seen the occasional tetrolimulus washed ashore to the south, where the creatures are feared as the twisted manifestations of Achaekek, conjured for worship by the Red Mantis and a stark reminder of the folly of religious devotion. There are descriptions of creatures similar to the tetrolimulus to the north, even into the Inner Sea, but these stories are as old and leaky as the ships of the pirates and traders who tell them and no reports of tetrolimuluses along the cost of Cheliax, for example, are younger than two generations.\n\nMuch of tetrolimuluses' bulk is armor, and despite their size they can survive on relatively small quantities of food. In perhaps the only mark of intelligence in their species, they try to avoid overfishing, instead roaming over several miles of coastline to balance their Ecology. The majority of their diet is fish and cephalopods, but they are competent trackers and follow hints of habitation on their beaches to devour any coast-dwelling mammals foolish enough to find themselves on the beaches, including humanoids. Like most animals, tetrolimuluses tend to avoid large settlements or areas frequently visited by humans. Remote or inaccessible beaches are the females' preferred habitat, but occasionally a powerful storm rolling out of the Eye of Abendego can toss them on more popular or even populous coastlines. Surprisingly high concentrations of the creatures are found around Mediogalti Island and its outlying cluster. Some suggest this is due to deliberate cultivation by the Red Mantis, thanks to the tetrolimulus's favorable form, but it may simply be because the treacherous waters and hidden coves are perfect for their reclusive lifestyle, and the frequent mutinies, shipwrecks, and foolish adventurers provide a varied and ample diet for the brutal predators.\n\nTetrodotoxin\n\nWhile none are stupid enough to actively farm sea-mantises, occasionally the corpse of one is washed up into the more accessible bays on the coasts of the Shackles or Mediogalti Island. Some of the more enterprising residents of Ilizmagorti have developed a method of harvesting the cruel tetrodotoxin poison, from which the tetrolimulus gets its name, for sale to the assassins of the Red Mantis.\n\nA single dose of tetrodotoxin sells for 1,300 gp. Its rarity and potency make it a valuable product, and prices outside the Shackles or Mediogalti Island can be 50-100% higher.\n\nOne dose of poison can be harvested from the corpse of a tetrolimulus, provided the lower half of the creature is intact. This requires a DC 25 Survival check, and even those who usually find themselves competent at skinning or gutting creatures struggle with the intricacies of the sharp tail stinger. In harvesting the tetrodotoxin poison, those without the poison use ability are subject to the standard 5% chance of self-poisoning.","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Thriae Seer","cr":11,"xp":12800,"alignment":"LN","size":"Medium","type":"monstrous humanoid","init":5,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"detect secret doors"},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":25,"ac_touch":15,"ac_flat_footed":20,"ac_mods":"+5 Dex, +10 natural","hp":133,"hd":"14d10+56","hdvalue":14,"fort":8,"ref":16,"will":5,"immunities":["poison","sonic"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10}],"sr":22,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":60,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"+2 quarterstaff +16 (1d6+4), +2 quarterstaff +16 (1d6+3), sting +11 (1d8+3 plus mind sting)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"merope consumption"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":14,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":22,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"detect secret doors"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"calm emotions"},{"spell":"detect thoughts"},{"spell":"sound burst"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"summon bees","details":"level 5, 1d3 giant queen bees or 1d4 wasp swarms"},{"spell":"true seeing"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"divination"},{"spell":"invisibility purge"},{"spell":"locate object"},{"spell":"misdirection"},{"spell":"symbol of sleep"}]}],"strength":14,"dexterity":20,"constitution":19,"intelligence":19,"wisdom":22,"charisma":27,"baseatk":14,"cmb":10,"cmd":23,"feats":[{"feat":"Agile Maneuvers"},{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Combat Casting"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Improved Two-Weapon Fighting"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Two-Weapon Fighting"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":22},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":22},{"skill":"Fly","value":26},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":18},{"skill":"Perception","value":27},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":24},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":18},{"skill":"Use Magic Device","value":22}],"languages":["Common","Sylvan","Thriae"],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","triad"],"treasure":"double (+2 quarterstaff, 3 doses of merope)","description_visual":"Lithe and beautiful, this half-bee, half-woman creature wears elaborate makeup and wields an ornate staff.","group":"Thriae","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 3","special_abilities":[{"type":"Merope Consumption","kind":"Su","details":"Three times per day as a standard action, a thriae seer can consume a dose of merope in order to further tap into her spiritual powers for 1d6+3 rounds. Starting on the round after she consumes the merope, the thriae seer gains an insight bonus to her AC and on damage done with melee attacks equal to her Wisdom modifier (+6 for most thriae seers)."},{"type":"Mind Sting","kind":"Su","details":"A target stung by a thriae seer becomes confused for 1d4 rounds unless it makes a successful DC 21 Will save. This is a mind-affecting effect. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"Sought after for their wisdom and guidance as well as their enchanting beauty, thriae seers are among the most spiritually gifted members of their colony. Their prowess for foretelling the future and deciding upon the soundest courses of action in dire situations earns them respect from other thriae as well as outsiders from other societies, and seers wield their gift with a stoic humbleness. Nonetheless, most seers expect an offering before they will grant an audience a divination. These offerings usually consist of ornate jewelry and sums of gold, though some seers desire the company of humanoid male or female consorts, many of whom gladly oblige the captivating seer with their presence.\n\nWhile their combative abilities mainly comprise their magical powers and they appear at first glance to be thin and frail, seers still possess the trademark strength and resilience of all thriae.\n\nThriae seers spend most of their time meditating in one of the many chambers in the colony's hive dedicated to such activities. Consuming large amounts of their queen's merope to enhance their powers of divination, seers ponder the best solutions to their colony's problems, and often act as a sort of spiritual political council for the queen. If a particularly wealthy group of outsiders has sought the counsel of several thriae seers, this council of prophetesses will combine their powers in order to read a difficult divination.\n\nThriae seers are 6 ft. from head to toe and weigh 150 pounds. The thriae seer presented here represents the least of her kind. Many thriae seers take levels of monk or rogue so as to be even more adept at protecting their queen. Thriae oracles and sorcerers are also relatively common-such thriae are particularly valued by their hive for their magical abilities.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Thunderbird","cr":11,"xp":12800,"alignment":"N","size":"Gargantuan","type":"magical beast","init":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"stormsight"}],"auras":["storm aura (100 ft.)"],"ac":25,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":21,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +1 dodge, +15 natural, -4 size","hp":147,"hd":"14d10+70","hdvalue":14,"fort":14,"ref":12,"will":7,"immunities":["electricity","sonic"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":120,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"2 claws +18  (2d6+8/19-20  plus grab), bite +18  (2d8+8/19-20)","ranged":"thunderbolt +13  ranged touch (6d6  electricity and 6d6 sonic)","space":"20 ft.","reach":"20 ft.","spell_like_abilities_caster_level":11,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":16,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"control weather"}]}],"strength":26,"dexterity":17,"constitution":21,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":16,"charisma":13,"baseatk":14,"cmb":23,"cmd":35,"feats":[{"feat":"Critical Focus"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (claw)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":13},{"skill":"Fly","value":11},{"skill":"Perception","value":20},{"skill":"Perform (sing)","value":8},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":10}],"languages":["Auran"],"environments":["any hills","any mountains"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This enormous bird has feathers the color of a stormy sky, a resemblance enhanced by the lightning that dances over its body.","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 2","special_abilities":[{"type":"Thunderbolt","kind":"Su","details":"A thunderbird can fire a ray of thunder and lightning from its outspread wings as a standard action. This attack has a range of 200 ft. with no range increment, and requires a ranged touch attack to hit. A creature critically hit by a thunderbolt is stunned and deafened for 1 round if it fails a DC 22 Fortitude save. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Storm Aura","kind":"Su","details":"A thunderbird is surrounded by a 100-footradius spread of severe winds that blow out from the center, dissipating swiftly at the limit of the aura's range. In this area, ranged weapons (but not siege weapons) take a -4 penalty on attack rolls, Fly checks are made at a -4 penalty, and exposed flames are extinguished. Small creatures must make a DC 10 Strength check (if on the ground) or a DC 20 Fly check to move toward the thunderbird, while Tiny or smaller creatures can be knocked backward (1d4 x 10 ft. if they are on the ground and fail a DC 15 Strength check, or 2d6 x 10 ft. if they are flying and fail a DC 25 Fly check). Creatures on the ground that are pushed back take 1d4 points of nonlethal damage per 10 ft., and flying creatures that are pushed back take 2d6 points of nonlethal damage regardless of the distance they are pushed. In addition, once every 1d4 rounds, a bolt of lightning strikes a random creature (other than the thunderbird) within the area of its storm aura. This bolt of lightning deals 12d6 points of electricity damage (DC 22 Reflex halves). The save DC for the lightning bolt is Constitutionbased, while those for resisting the wind effects are fixed."},{"type":"Stormsight","kind":"Ex","details":"A thunderbird ignores all vision penalties and concealment from weather effects, including those created by fog cloud, obscuring mist, and similar spells."}],"description":"Thunderbirds bring the storm on their wings. In times of drought, they are welcomed with joy and celebration.\n\nIn other times, they are placated with gifts in hopes that they might leave quickly before flooding begins. When angered, thunderbirds can call down hurricanes and lay waste to entire villages, so in regions where these birds dwell, many villages maintain extensive rituals designed to appease and honor the local thunderbirds.\n\nThunderbirds nest near the base of waterfalls, where the constant thrum of crashing water prepares the hatchlings for a life at the heart of a storm. Once the chicks have hatched, their parents carry the offspring to nests at the top of mountains, where the young are struck by their first bolts of lightning and learn the mysteries of the storm.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"White Rider","cr":11,"xp":12800,"alignment":"LN","size":"Medium","type":"fey","init":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"auras":["blinding light (30 ft., DC 23)"],"ac":27,"ac_touch":17,"ac_flat_footed":20,"ac_mods":"+6 armor, +7 Dex, +4 natural","hp":136,"hd":"16d6+80","hdvalue":16,"fort":10,"ref":17,"will":15,"dr":"10/cold iron","immunities":["cold","poison"],"sr":22,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"+1 longsword +14 (1d8+6/19-20)","ranged":"+2 seeking composite longbow +18 (1d8+7/19-20/3)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"Rider's weapon"},{"type":"weal or woe","details":"DC 23"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":11,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":16,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"see invisibility"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"chill touch"},{"spell":"detect thoughts"},{"spell":"zone of truth"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"mass suggestion"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"charm monster"},{"spell":"cone of cold"}]},{"frequency":"5/day","spells":[{"spell":"daybreak arrow"},{"spell":"ice storm"}]}],"strength":20,"dexterity":25,"constitution":20,"intelligence":18,"wisdom":21,"charisma":21,"baseatk":8,"cmb":13,"cmd":23,"feats":[{"feat":"Improved Critical (composite longbow)"},{"feat":"Manyshot"},{"feat":"Mounted Archery"},{"feat":"Mounted Combat"},{"feat":"Point-Blank Shot"},{"feat":"Precise Shot"},{"feat":"Rapid Shot"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (composite longbow)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":18},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":23},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":20},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":18},{"skill":"Knowledge (history)","value":18},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":21},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":18},{"skill":"Perception","value":24},{"skill":"Ride","value":26},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":24},{"skill":"Stealth","value":26}],"languages":["Common","Hallit","Skald","Sylvan","telepathy 60 ft."],"sq":[{"type":"conjure mount"},{"type":"Rider's robes"}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"A tall, handsome woman sits astride a white horse. She grips an elegant longbow made of raw birch.","group":"The White Rider","source":"Irrisen Land Of Eternal Winter","special_abilities":[{"type":"Blinding Light","kind":"Su","details":"The White Rider can radiate a 30-foot-radius aura of blinding light as a free action. Creatures within the affected area must succeed at a DC 23 Fortitude save or be permanently blinded. A creature that successfully saves cannot be affected again by the Rider's blinding light aura for 24 hours. The save is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Rider's Robes","kind":"Su","details":"The White Rider wears robes that provide the same protection as a breastplate."},{"type":"Rider's Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"The White Rider has a +2 seeking composite longbow and a quiver that produces a never-ending supply of arrows. Once per round, she can draw a +1 brilliant energy arrow from her quiver."}],"description":"The White Rider is the most even-tempered and diplomatic of the Three Riders. This doesn't mean that she is sympathetic or merciful, just that there is less blood staining the crisp white garments she wears. When the White Rider comes calling, citizens of Irrisen often seek to curry favor by bringing her gifts of hot tea, pastries, and fresh baked bread. She rarely accepts these offerings, and when she does it is only from those she has already judged to be loyal to Baba Yaga and worthy of the Queen of Witches's rule. Those who too eagerly attempt to carry favor face added scrutiny from her.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","gear":"+1 longsword"},{"name":"Young Adult Copper Dragon","cr":11,"xp":12800,"alignment":"CG","size":"Large","type":"dragon","subtypes":["earth"],"init":5,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"}],"ac":26,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":25,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +16 natural, -1 size","hp":136,"hd":"13d12+52","hdvalue":13,"fort":12,"ref":9,"will":11,"defensive_abilities":["uncanny dodge"],"dr":"5/magic","immunities":["acid","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":22,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"speed_mod":"climb stone","melee":"bite +18 (2d6+9/19-20), 2 claws +18 (1d8+6/19-20), tail slap +13 (1d8+9), 2 wings +13 (1d6+3)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft. (10 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"80-ft. line, DC 20, 10d6 acid"},{"type":"slow breath"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":13,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":17,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"grease"},{"spell":"hideous laughter"}]}],"spellsknown_caster":"sorcerer","spellsknown_caster_level":5,"spellsknown_concentration":9,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"invisibility"},{"spell":"phantom trap"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"alarm"},{"spell":"magic missile"},{"spell":"shield"},{"spell":"silent image"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"ghost sound"},{"spell":"light"},{"spell":"message"},{"spell":"prestidigitation"},{"spell":"read magic"}]}],"strength":23,"dexterity":12,"constitution":19,"intelligence":16,"wisdom":17,"charisma":16,"baseatk":13,"cmb":20,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. trip","cmd":31,"cmd_special":"+6 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Combat Expertise"},{"feat":"Greater Trip"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite, claw)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Trip"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":19},{"skill":"Craft (traps)","value":24},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":19},{"skill":"Fly","value":11},{"skill":"Perception","value":19,"special":"+24 vs. traps"},{"skill":"Perform (comedy)","value":16},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":19},{"skill":"Stealth","value":13},{"skill":"Use Magic Device","value":19}],"languages":["Common","Draconic","Gnome","Halfling"],"sq":[{"type":"trap master"}],"environments":["warm hills"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"Bright, shining copper scales run from the horn-crowned head to the ridged tail of this long-winged dragon.","group":"Metallic Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Climb Stone","kind":"Ex","details":"A copper dragon can climb on stone surfaces as though using the spider climb spell."},{"type":"Slow Breath","kind":"Su","details":"Instead of a line of acid, a copper dragon can breathe a cone of slowing gas. Those in the cone must make a Fortitude save or be slowed (as per the spell slow) for 1d6 rounds plus 1 round per age category of the dragon."},{"type":"Trap Master","kind":"Ex","details":"A juvenile or older copper dragon receives a +1 bonus per age categroy on Craft (traps) and Perception checks made to locate a trap. Upon becoming a mature adult, he can also use Disable Device to disarm magic traps as if he had the rogue's Trapfinding class feature."}],"description":"This whimsical dragon spends most of its time in combat trying to annoy and frustrate its enemies.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Young Adult Green Dragon","cr":11,"xp":12800,"alignment":"LE","size":"Huge","type":"dragon","subtypes":["air"],"init":0,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"}],"auras":["frightful presence (150 ft., DC 18)"],"ac":24,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":24,"ac_mods":"+16 natural, -2 size","hp":136,"hd":"13d12+52","hdvalue":13,"fort":12,"ref":8,"will":12,"dr":"5/magic","immunities":["acid","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":22,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"},{"type":"swim","speed":40}],"melee":"bite +18 (2d8+10/19-20), 2 claws +18 (2d6+7/19-20), 2 wings +13 (1d8+3), tail slap +13 (2d6+10)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"50-ft. cone, DC 20, 10d6 acid"},{"type":"crush","details":"Small creatures, DC 20, 2d8+10"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":13,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":17,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"charm person"},{"spell":"entangle"}]}],"spellsknown_caster_level":3,"spellsknown_concentration":7,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":6,"spells":[{"spell":"shield"},{"spell":"silent image"},{"spell":"summon monster I"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"dancing lights"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"ghost sound"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"prestidigitation"}]}],"strength":25,"dexterity":10,"constitution":19,"intelligence":14,"wisdom":15,"charisma":14,"baseatk":13,"cmb":22,"cmd":32,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (claws)"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":8},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":18},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":18},{"skill":"Perception","value":22},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":18},{"skill":"Stealth","value":8},{"skill":"Survival","value":18},{"skill":"Swim","value":31}],"languages":["Common","Draconic","Elven"],"sq":[{"type":"water breathing"},{"type":"woodland stride"}],"environments":["temperate forests"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"Scales the color of emeralds armor this ferocious dragon. A single sharp horn protrudes from the end of its toothy snout.","group":"Chromatic Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Water Breathing","kind":"Ex","details":"A green dragon can breathe underwater indefinitely and can freely use its breath weapon, spells, and other abilities while submerged."},{"type":"Woodland Stride","kind":"Ex","details":"A very young or older green dragon can move through any sort of foliage at full speed without taking damage or suffering impairment. Areas of foliage that have been magically manipulated affect it normally."}],"description":"Green dragons dwell in the ancient forests of the world, prowling under towering canopies in search of prey. Of all the chromatic dragons, green dragons are perhaps the easiest to deal with diplomatically.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Young Gold Dragon","cr":11,"xp":12800,"alignment":"LG","size":"Large","type":"dragon","subtypes":["fire"],"init":1,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"}],"ac":23,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":22,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +13 natural, -1 size","hp":126,"hd":"12d12+48","hdvalue":12,"fort":12,"ref":9,"will":13,"immunities":["fire","paralysis","sleep"],"weaknesses":["vulnerability to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":60},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"},{"type":"swim","speed":60}],"melee":"bite +18 (2d6+10), 2 claws +18 (1d8+7/19-20), 2 wings +16 (1d6+3), tail +16 (1d8+10)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft. (10 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"40-ft. cone, DC 20, 6d10 fire"},{"type":"weakening breath"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":12,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":16,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"detect evil"}]}],"spellsknown_caster_level":1,"spellsknown_concentration":5,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":4,"spells":[{"spell":"mage armor"},{"spell":"shield"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"light"},{"spell":"mending"},{"spell":"stabilize"}]}],"strength":25,"dexterity":12,"constitution":19,"intelligence":16,"wisdom":17,"charisma":16,"baseatk":12,"cmb":20,"cmd":31,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (claw)"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":18},{"skill":"Fly","value":10},{"skill":"Heal","value":18},{"skill":"Knowledge (local, religion)","value":18},{"skill":"Perception","value":22},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":22},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":18},{"skill":"Swim","value":30}],"languages":["Common","Draconic","Elven","Halfling"],"sq":[{"type":"change shape"},{"type":"detect gems"},{"type":"fast flight"}],"environments":["warm plains"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"Golden scales cover the body of this majestic dragon, and a regal crest of horns arches backward above wise and piercing eyes.","group":"Metallic Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Change Shape","kind":"Su","details":"A very young or older gold dragon can assume any animal or humanoid form three times per day as if using polymorph."},{"type":"Detect Gems","kind":"Sp","details":"A young or older gold dragon can detect gems three times per day. This functions as locate object, but can only be used to locate gemstones."},{"type":"Divine Aid","kind":"Sp","details":"Once a week, a great wyrm gold dragon can call upon celestial powers for aid. This functions as a miracle."},{"type":"Fast Flight","kind":"Ex","details":"A young or older gold dragon is treated as one size category larger when determining his fly speed."},{"type":"Fire Aura","kind":"Su","details":"An old or older gold dragon is surrounded by an aura of fire. All creatures within 5 ft. of the dragon take 1d6 points of fire damage at the beginning of the dragon's turn. An ancient gold dragon's aura extends to 10 ft. A great wyrm's damage increases to 2d6. The dragon can activate or suppress this aura as a free action."},{"type":"Luck","kind":"Sp","details":"Once per day an adult or older gold dragon can touch a gem, usually one embedded in the dragon's hide, and enspell it to bring good luck. As long as the dragon carries the gem, it and every good creature within a given radius of it (10 ft. per age category) receives a +1 luck bonus on all saving throws. If the dragon gives an enspelled gem to another creature, only that bearer gets the bonus. The effect lasts 1d3 hours plus 3 hours per age category of the dragon. This ability is the equivalent of a 2nd-level spell."},{"type":"Spell-Like Abilities","kind":"Sp","details":"A gold dragon gains the following spell-like abilities upon reaching the listed age category. Its caster level for these effects is equal to its Hit Dice, and any save DCs are Charisma-based. A gold dragon can use these abilities at will. Very young-detect evil; Juvenile-bless; Adult-daylight; Old-geas/quest; Ancient-sunburst; Great wyrm-foresight."},{"type":"Weakening Breath","kind":"Su","details":"Instead of a cone of fire, a gold dragon can breathe a cone of weakening gas. Creatures within the cone must succeed on a Fortitude save or take 1 point of Strength damage per age category (Will save half). Age Category S pecial Abilities C aster Level Wyrmling Fire subtype, weakening breath - Very young Change shape, detect evil - Young Fast flight, detect gems 1st Juvenile Bless 3rd Young adult DR 5/magic, spell resistance 5th Adult Frightful presence, luck, daylight 7th Mature adult DR 10/magic 9th Old Fire aura, geas/quest 11th Very old DR 15/magic 13th Ancient Sunburst 15th Wyrm DR 20/magic 17th Great wyrm Divine aid, foresight 19th  A gold dragon can cast cleric spells as arcane spells."}],"description":"Gold dragons are the epitome of virtue. Other metallic dragons revere their gold cousins as the agents of divine forces and the paragons of dragonkind, and often seek them for advice or aid.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Young Sovereign Dragon","cr":11,"xp":12800,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"dragon","init":5,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"}],"ac":23,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":22,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +13 natural, -1 size","hp":126,"hd":"12d12+48","hdvalue":12,"fort":12,"ref":11,"will":13,"immunities":["paralysis","sleep"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"bite +19 (2d6+10), 2 claws +18 (1d8+7), gore +18 (1d8+10), tail slap +16 (1d8+10)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft. (10 ft. with bite and gore)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"40-ft. cone, 6d6 sonic damage, DC 20"},{"type":"violent retort"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":12,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":16,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"detect good/evil"}]}],"spellsknown_caster_level":1,"spellsknown_concentration":5,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":4,"spells":[{"spell":"charm person"},{"spell":"color spray"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"daze"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"read magic"},{"spell":"resistance"}]}],"strength":25,"dexterity":12,"constitution":19,"intelligence":16,"wisdom":17,"charisma":16,"baseatk":12,"cmb":20,"cmd":31,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Persuasive"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Appraise","value":18},{"skill":"Bluff","value":18},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":22},{"skill":"Fly","value":-3},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":22},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana, history)","value":18},{"skill":"Perception","value":18},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":18},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":18}],"languages":["Celestial","Common","Draconic","Infernal"],"sq":[{"type":"change shape"},{"type":"dogmatic discordance"}],"environments":["any mountains"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"This magnificent dragon is covered in splendid gold scales, and horns jut from its head like a crown.","group":"Imperial Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 3","special_abilities":[{"type":"Change Shape","kind":"Su","details":"A young or older sovereign dragon can assume any humanoid form three times per day as polymorph."},{"type":"Dogmatic Discordance","kind":"Su","details":"Good or evil creatures take a -2 penalty when making saving throws against a sovereign dragon's spells, spell-like abilities, breath weapon, and aura."},{"type":"Golden Armor","kind":"Su","details":"Once per day as a standard action, an old or older sovereign dragon can cover its form in golden armor, granting it a +4 armor bonus to AC and energy resistance 15 to one energy type, chosen at the time the armor is summoned. This armor lasts for a number of rounds equal to the dragon's age category. The sovereign dragon can dismiss the armor as a free action."},{"type":"Master Counterspelling","kind":"Su","details":"A great wyrm sovereign dragon can counterspell once per round as an immediate action. It need not know the spell it is countering, but can instead expend any spell that is one level higher to automatically counter the spell."},{"type":"Violent Retort","kind":"Ex","details":"When a young or older sovereign dragon takes damage from a melee attack critical hit, it can, as an immediate action, make a claw or tail slap attack against the creature that made the critical hit."}],"description":"Guardians of balance, sovereign dragons, or lungwangs as they are also known, were placed in the skies by the gods themselves to safeguard harmony in the world.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Young Time Dragon","cr":11,"xp":12800,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"dragon","init":9,"senses":[{"type":"detect magic"},{"type":"dragon senses"},{"type":"see in darkness"}],"ac":21,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":19,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +10 natural, -1 size","hp":149,"hd":"13d12+65","hdvalue":13,"fort":13,"ref":10,"will":10,"immunities":["cold","paralysis","sleep","staggered"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"bite +20 (2d6+10), 2 claws +20 (1d8+7), 2 wings +17 (1d6+3), tail slap +17 (1d8+10)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft. (10 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"40-ft. cone, 6d10 electricity, DC 21"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":11,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":16,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"detect magic"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"share memory"}]}],"spellsknown_caster":"sorcerer","spellsknown_caster_level":1,"spellsknown_concentration":6,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":4,"spells":[{"spell":"erase"},{"spell":"mage armor"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"message"},{"spell":"read magic"},{"spell":"resistance"}]}],"strength":24,"dexterity":15,"constitution":20,"intelligence":15,"wisdom":14,"charisma":15,"baseatk":13,"cmb":21,"cmd":33,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Knowledge [history])"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (claw)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":18},{"skill":"Fly","value":12},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":18},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":18},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":18},{"skill":"Knowledge (history)","value":24},{"skill":"Perception","value":18},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":18}],"languages":["Common","Draconic","Elven"],"sq":[{"type":"immortal"},{"type":"no breath"},{"type":"read the threads"},{"type":"starflight"}],"environments":["any vacuum"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"This dragon's cracked scales creak with frightening, patient power. Some of its horns are ancient and brittle, others new and pristine.","group":"Outer Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 4","special_abilities":[{"type":"Immortal","kind":"Ex","details":"Time dragons age, but don't die from old age."},{"type":"Read the Threads","kind":"Su","details":"A time dragon gains a racial bonus on initiative checks equal to its age category. In addition, a time dragon is immune to the staggered condition."},{"type":"Alien Presence","kind":"Su","details":"A creature that fails its saving throw against a time dragon's alien presence is staggered for 5d6 rounds (or stunned if it has 4 Hit Dice or fewer)."},{"type":"Shifting Breath","kind":"Su","details":"Instead of a cone of electricity, an old or older time dragon can use its breath weapon to displace creatures in time. Each creature in the cone must succeed at a Will save or be shifted forward in time a number of rounds equal to 1/2 the dragon's age category (DC equal to breath weapon). For an affected creature, it's as if no time passed. Creatures that succeed at their saves are staggered for 1 round."},{"type":"Second Chance","kind":"Su","details":"Three times per day as an immediate action, an ancient or older time dragon can force a creature (including itself) to reroll any d20 roll. The target must use the result of the second roll."},{"type":"Time Travel","kind":"Su","details":"Up to three times in its life, a great wyrm time dragon can travel to any point in time, taking with it a number of willing creatures equal to its Charisma modifier."}],"description":"Guardians of history, time dragons are the most powerful of the outer dragons. Watchers and waiters, time dragons guard the universe against those that would interfere with the natural temporal order.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Adult Copper Dragon","cr":12,"xp":19200,"alignment":"CG","size":"Large","type":"dragon","subtypes":["earth"],"init":5,"auras":["frightful presence (180 ft., DC 21)"],"ac":29,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":28,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +19 natural, -1 size","hp":172,"hd":"15d12+75","hdvalue":15,"fort":14,"ref":10,"will":13,"defensive_abilities":["uncanny dodge"],"dr":"5/magic","immunities":["acid","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":23,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"speed_mod":"climb stone","melee":"bite +21 (2d6+10/19-20), 2 claws +21 (1d8+7/19-20), 2 wings +16 (1d6+3), tail +16 (1d8+10)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft. (10 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"b. weapon","details":"80-ft. line, DC 22, 12d6 acid"},{"type":"slow breath"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":15,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":20,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"grease"},{"spell":"hideous laughter"},{"spell":"stone shape"}]}],"spellsknown_caster_level":7,"spellsknown_concentration":12,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"major image"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"glitterdust"},{"spell":"invisibility"},{"spell":"phantom trap"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"alarm"},{"spell":"identify"},{"spell":"magic missile"},{"spell":"shield"},{"spell":"silent image"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"ghost sound"},{"spell":"light"},{"spell":"message"},{"spell":"open/close"},{"spell":"prestidigitation"},{"spell":"read magic"}]}],"strength":25,"dexterity":12,"constitution":21,"intelligence":18,"wisdom":19,"charisma":18,"baseatk":15,"cmb":23,"cmd":34,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Combat Expertise"},{"feat":"Greater Trip"},{"feat":"Improved Critcal (bite, claw)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Trip"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":22},{"skill":"Craft (traps)","value":28},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":22},{"skill":"Fly","value":13},{"skill":"Perception","value":22},{"skill":"Perform (comedy)","value":19},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":22},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":22},{"skill":"Stealth","value":15},{"skill":"Use Magic Device","value":22}],"languages":["Common","Draconic","Elven","Gnome","Halfling"],"sq":[{"type":"trap master"}],"environments":["warm hills"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"Bright, shining copper scales run from the horn-crowned head to the ridged tail of this long-winged dragon.","group":"Metallic Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Climb Stone","kind":"Ex","details":"A copper dragon can climb on stone surfaces as though using the spider climb spell."},{"type":"Deadly Joke","kind":"Sp","details":"Once per day, as a standard action, a great wyrm copper dragon can tell a joke that kills. This affects one target, and functions as power word kill. This is a language-dependent sonic effect."},{"type":"Mass Laughter","kind":"Sp","details":"An ancient copper dragon can tell a fantastic joke once per day as a standard action. All creatures within 10 ft. per age category must make a Will save or laugh for 1 round per age category, as if affected by hideous laughter. The save DC is Charisma-based. This is equal to a 6th-level spell."},{"type":"Slow Aura","kind":"Su","details":"An old or older copper dragon is surrounded by an aura of slowness. All creatures within 5 ft. of the dragon must make a Will save or be affected as per slow for 1 round. An ancient dragon's aura extends to 10 ft. For great wyrm copper dragons, those opponents that fail their saves are slowed for 1d4 rounds. The DC of this save is equal to the dragon's breath weapon. A copper dragon can suppress or activate this aura at will as a free action."},{"type":"Slow Breath","kind":"Su","details":"Instead of a line of acid, a copper dragon can breathe a cone of slowing gas. Those in the cone must make a Fortitude save or be slowed (as per the spell slow) for 1d6 rounds plus 1 round per age category of the dragon."},{"type":"Spell-Like Abilities","kind":"Sp","details":"A copper dragon gains the following spell-like abilities, usable at will upon reaching the listed age category. Very young-grease; Juvenile-hideous laughter; Adult-stone shape; Old-transmute rock to mud/mud to rock; Ancient-wall of stone; Great wyrm-move earth."},{"type":"Trap Master","kind":"Ex","details":"A juvenile or older copper dragon receives a +1 bonus per age categroy on Craft (traps) and Perception checks made to locate a trap. Upon becoming a mature adult, he can also use Disable Device to disarm magic traps as if he had the rogue's Trapfinding class feature."},{"type":"Uncanny Dodge","kind":"Ex","details":"A young or older copper dragon is always looking out for an ambush. He can never be caught flat-footed. This ability functions like the rogue ability of the same name. Age Category S pecial Abilities C aster Level Wyrmling Immunity to acid, climb stone, - slow breath Very young Grease - Young Uncanny dodge 1st Juvenile Trap master, hideous laughter 3rd Young adult DR 5/magic, spell resistance 5th Adult Frightful presence, stone shape 7th Mature adult DR 10/magic 9th Old Slow aura, transmute rock/mud 11th Very old DR 15/magic 13th Ancient Mass laughter, wall of stone 15th Wyrm DR 20/magic 17th Great wyrm Deadly joke, move earth 19th."}],"description":"This whimsical dragon spends most of its time in combat trying to annoy and frustrate its enemies.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Adult Green Dragon","cr":12,"xp":19200,"alignment":"LE","size":"Huge","type":"dragon","subtypes":["air"],"init":0,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"}],"auras":["frightful presence (180 ft., DC 20)"],"ac":27,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":27,"ac_mods":"+19 natural, -2 size","hp":172,"hd":"15d12+75","hdvalue":15,"fort":14,"ref":9,"will":14,"dr":"5/magic","immunities":["acid","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":23,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"},{"type":"swim","speed":40}],"melee":"bite +21 (2d8+12/19-20), 2 claws +21 (2d6+8/19-20), 2 wings +16 (1d8+4), tail slap +16 (2d6+12)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"50-ft. cone, DC 22, 12d6 acid"},{"type":"crush","details":"Small creatures, DC 22, 2d8+12"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":15,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":20,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"charm person"},{"spell":"entangle"},{"spell":"suggestion"}]}],"spellsknown_caster_level":5,"spellsknown_concentration":10,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"alter self"},{"spell":"mirror image"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"shield"},{"spell":"silent image"},{"spell":"summon monster I"},{"spell":"ventriloquism"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"dancing lights"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"ghost sound"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"message"},{"spell":"prestidigitation"}]}],"strength":27,"dexterity":10,"constitution":21,"intelligence":16,"wisdom":17,"charisma":16,"baseatk":15,"cmb":25,"cmd":35,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite, claws)"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":10},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcane)","value":21},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":21},{"skill":"Perception","value":25},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":21},{"skill":"Stealth","value":10},{"skill":"Survival","value":21},{"skill":"Swim","value":34},{"skill":"Use Magic Device","value":21}],"languages":["Common","Draconic","Elven","Sylvan"],"sq":[{"type":"trackless step"},{"type":"water breathing"},{"type":"woodland stride"}],"environments":["temperate forests"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"Scales the color of emeralds armor this ferocious dragon. A single sharp horn protrudes from the end of its toothy snout.","group":"Chromatic Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Awaken Treants","kind":"Su","details":"A great wyrm dragon can call on the forest itself to aid it, animating a number of trees to serve as treants to protect it. These treants can be called from any Huge or larger living tree. A green dragon can create a single treant as a standard action, up to a total of 4 treants per day. These treants remain animated for up to 1 hour, at which time they revert to being ordinary trees."},{"type":"Camouflage","kind":"Ex","details":"An old or older green dragon can use Stealth to hide in any sort of natural terrain, even if the terrain doesn't grant cover or concealment."},{"type":"Miasma","kind":"Su","details":"An ancient or older green dragon can use its breath weapon to create a cloud of acid as a standard action that deals damage to any creature inside it. The cloud moves with the dragon and has a radius of 20 ft. When it's created, anyone inside this area takes an amount of damage equal to half the dragon's breath weapon, with a Reflex save for half damage. The number of damage dice rolled is halved each round until the result would be less than 1d6. Any creature that starts its turn inside the cloud takes damage, but can make a Reflex save for half. A strong wind, such as that created by a gust of wind, disperses the cloud in 1 round."},{"type":"Spell-Like Abilities","kind":"Sp","details":"A green dragon gains the following spell-like abilities, usable at will upon reaching the listed age category. Young-entangle; Juvenile-charm person; Adult-suggestion; Old-plant growth; Ancient-dominate person; Great wyrm-command plants."},{"type":"Trackless Step","kind":"Ex","details":"An adult or older green dragon doesn't leave a trail in natural surroundings and cannot be tracked. A green dragon can choose to leave a trail, if it so desires."},{"type":"Water Breathing","kind":"Ex","details":"A green dragon can breathe underwater indefinitely and can freely use its breath weapon, spells, and other abilities while submerged."},{"type":"Woodland Stride","kind":"Ex","details":"A very young or older green dragon can move through any sort of foliage at full speed without taking damage or suffering impairment. Areas of foliage that have been magically manipulated affect it normally. Age Category S pecial Abilities Caster Level Wyrmling Immunity to acid, water breathing - Very young Woodland stride - Young Entangle - Juvenile Frightful presence, charm person 1st Young adult DR 5/magic, spell resistance 3rd Adult Trackless step, suggestion 5th Mature adult DR 10/magic 7th Old Camouflage, plant growth 9th Very old DR 15/magic 11th Ancient Miasma, dominate person 13th Wyrm DR 20/magic 15th Great wyrm Awaken treants, command plants 17th."}],"description":"Green dragons dwell in the ancient forests of the world, prowling under towering canopies in search of prey. Of all the chromatic dragons, green dragons are perhaps the easiest to deal with diplomatically.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Adult Magma Dragon","cr":12,"xp":19200,"alignment":"CN","size":"Large","type":"dragon","subtypes":["extraplanar","fire"],"init":5,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"}],"auras":["frightful presence (180 ft., DC 20)"],"ac":29,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":28,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +19 natural, -1 size","hp":172,"hd":"15d12+75","hdvalue":15,"fort":16,"ref":10,"will":15,"dr":"5/magic","immunities":["fire","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":23,"weaknesses":["vulnerable to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"bite +22 (2d6+12/19-20 plus 6 fire), 2 claws +22 (1d8+8/19-20), tail slap +17 (1d8+12), 2 wings +17 (1d6+4)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft. (10 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"40-ft. cone, 12d6 fire, DC 22"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":15,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":20,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"burning hands"},{"spell":"scorching ray"},{"spell":"wall of fire"}]}],"spellsknown_caster_level":7,"spellsknown_concentration":12,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"fireball"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"dust of twilight"},{"spell":"flaming sphere"},{"spell":"glitterdust"},{"spell":"pyrotechnics"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"feather fall"},{"spell":"flare burst"},{"spell":"grease"},{"spell":"shield"},{"spell":"true strike"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"bleed"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"detect poison"},{"spell":"open/ close"},{"spell":"read magic"},{"spell":"spark"},{"spell":"touch of fatigue"}]}],"strength":27,"dexterity":12,"constitution":21,"intelligence":18,"wisdom":18,"charisma":17,"baseatk":15,"cmb":24,"cmd":35,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (claws)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":16,"special":"+20 jump"},{"skill":"Climb","value":26},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":16},{"skill":"Fly","value":13},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":21},{"skill":"Perception","value":22},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":22},{"skill":"Sleight of Hand","value":16},{"skill":"Stealth","value":15},{"skill":"Swim","value":26}],"languages":["Common","Draconic","Dwarven","Elven","Ignan"],"sq":[{"type":"superheated"}],"environments":["any mountains (Plane of Fire)","any underground (Plane of Fire)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"Between this dragon's jet-black scales run glowing rivulets of lava, and veins aglow with heat shine in the membranes of its wings.","group":"Primal Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 2","special_abilities":[{"type":"Magma Tomb","kind":"Su","details":"Once per day, a great wyrm magma dragon can spit lava onto a target within 120 ft., dealing damage normally for its breath weapon. This magma cools instantly-it doesn't continue doing damage at this point but does entrap the victim (DC equals the dragon's breath weapon save DC, 3d6 minutes, hardness 8, hp 45)."},{"type":"Magma Breath","kind":"Su","details":"Three times per day, an ancient or older magma dragon can breathe a cone of lava instead of fire. The damage is unchanged, but the magma clings to those it damages, dealing half damage each round thereafter for 1d3 rounds. After this magma cools, it crumbles to dust."},{"type":"Spell-Like Abilities","kind":"Sp","details":"A magma dragon gains the following spell-like abilities, usable at will (unless indicated otherwise) on reaching the listed age category. Very young-burning hands; Juvenile-scorching ray; Adult- wall of fire; Old-fire shield (warm shield, constant); Ancient-delayed blast fireball (3/day); Great wyrm-wall of lava."},{"type":"Superheated","kind":"Su","details":"At young age and older, a magma dragon's bite attack deals additional fire damage equal to its age category."}],"description":"Temperamental and prone to violent outbursts, magma dragons are regarded by most other dragons as dangerously insane-an assumption that, more often than not, proves correct. One can rarely predict a magma dragon's state of mind until it either attacks or attempts to engage in conversation. For their part, magma dragons can justify all of their actions-they just rarely feel the need to do so.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Adult Sea Dragon","cr":12,"xp":19200,"alignment":"CG","size":"Huge","type":"dragon","subtypes":["water"],"init":4,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"}],"auras":["frightful presence (180 ft., DC 22)"],"ac":28,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":28,"ac_mods":"+20 natural, -2 size","hp":172,"hd":"15d12+75","hdvalue":15,"fort":16,"ref":11,"will":14,"dr":"5/magic","immunities":["electricity","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":23,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"},{"type":"swim","speed":80}],"melee":"bite +22 (2d8+12), 2 claws +22 (2d6+8), gore +21 (2d6+12), tail slap +19 (2d6+12)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite and gore)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"50-ft. cone, 12d6 fire damage, DC 22"},{"type":"crush","details":"DC 22, 2d8+12"},{"type":"torrent breath"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":15,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":20,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"call lightning"},{"spell":"create water"},{"spell":"hydraulic push"}]}],"spellsknown_caster_level":7,"spellsknown_concentration":12,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"hold person"},{"spell":"sleet storm"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"gust of wind"},{"spell":"mirror image"},{"spell":"see invisibility"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":8,"spells":[{"spell":"charm person"},{"spell":"chill touch"},{"spell":"color spray"},{"spell":"expeditious retreat"},{"spell":"sleep"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"acid splash"},{"spell":"daze"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"ray of frost"},{"spell":"read magic"},{"spell":"resistance"}]}],"strength":27,"dexterity":10,"constitution":21,"intelligence":20,"wisdom":21,"charisma":20,"baseatk":15,"cmb":25,"cmd":35,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Lunge"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite and claw)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":23},{"skill":"Fly","value":10},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":23},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":23},{"skill":"Knowledge (geography)","value":23},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":23},{"skill":"Perception","value":27},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":27},{"skill":"Stealth","value":10},{"skill":"Survival","value":23},{"skill":"Swim","value":34}],"languages":["Aquan","Auran","Celestial","Common","Draconic","Elven"],"sq":[{"type":"change shape"},{"type":"unfettered swimmer"},{"type":"water breathing"}],"environments":["any water"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"The long, undulating body of this serpentine dragon rolls and bends with scales the color of the ocean's waves.","group":"Imperial Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 3","special_abilities":[{"type":"Change Shape","kind":"Su","details":"A young or older sea dragon can assume any humanoid form three times per day as if using polymorph."},{"type":"Sea Strider","kind":"Su","details":"Three times per day as a standard action, an old or older sea dragon can move from one body of water to another as if using the teleport spell (self only)."},{"type":"Tidal Wave","kind":"Su","details":"Once per day, a great wyrm sea dragon can create a tidal wave. This ability is the same as the bronze dragon's ability of the same name."},{"type":"Torrent Breath","kind":"Su","details":"Instead of a cone of super-heated steam, a very young or older sea dragon can breathe a line of pressurized water twice the length of the sea dragon's cone breath weapon. This line deals bludgeoning damage."},{"type":"Unfettered Swimmer","kind":"Su","details":"A juvenile sea dragon gains a 10-foot bonus to its swim speed. The sea dragon's swim speed continues to increase by an additional 10 ft. every two age categories. Furthermore, while swimming, the sea dragon is treated as if under the effects of the spell freedom of movement."}],"description":"Infused with the power of waves and storms, sea dragons—or jiaolungs, as they are known in many lands-are draconic protectors of oceans and their creatures. Possessing tempestuous natures, sea dragons wander widely, sometimes claiming thousands of miles of ocean and coastlines as their protectorates.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Akhana","cr":12,"xp":19200,"alignment":"N","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["aeon","extraplanar"],"init":10,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"deathwatch"}],"ac":27,"ac_touch":18,"ac_flat_footed":21,"ac_mods":"+2 deflection, +6 Dex, +9 natural","hp":148,"hd":"11d10+88","hdvalue":11,"hp_mods":["fast healing 5"],"fort":17,"ref":11,"will":14,"immunities":["cold","critical hits","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"electricity","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":23,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":40,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"4 claws +16 (1d4+5 plus grab)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"soul siphoning"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":11,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":19,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"deathwatch"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"cure serious wounds"},{"spell":"gentle repose"},{"spell":"inflict serious wounds"},{"spell":"sanctuary"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"raise dead"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"restoration"},{"spell":"slay living"}]}],"strength":21,"dexterity":23,"constitution":26,"intelligence":16,"wisdom":21,"charisma":18,"baseatk":11,"cmb":16,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":34,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Hover"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":18},{"skill":"Fly","value":2},{"skill":"Heal","value":19},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":18},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":22},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":22},{"skill":"Perception","value":19},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":19},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":17},{"skill":"Stealth","value":20}],"languages":["envisaging"],"sq":[{"type":"extension of all"},{"type":"void form"}],"environments":["any (Outer Planes)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","collective (3-6)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"Four gray arms project from a swirling mass resembling a giant eye, from which a tail-like appendage dangles.","group":"Aeon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 2","special_abilities":[{"type":"Soul Siphoning","kind":"Su","details":"As a swift action, an akhana can use its tail to siphon life essence from a grappled foe. At the start of the aeon's turn, the victim gains 1d4 negative levels (a DC 23 Fortitude save negates and grants immunity to this akhana's soul siphoning ability for 24 hours). When the number of negative levels equals the target's Hit Dice, the target's soul tears free from its mortal body and gets stored within the body of the akhana as a trap the soul spell. The victim's body remains preserved as if via a gentle repose spell for as long as the soul is held by the akhana. The akhana can keep the soul indefinitely, or can release it as a full-round action. Upon doing so, the released soul immediately returns to its body if the body is within 300 ft., at which point the body returns to life and any negative levels imparted to it by the akhana are removed. If the body isn't within 300 ft. (or if it has been destroyed), then the creature dies when its soul is released. A miracle, limited wish, or wish can force a displaced soul to return to its proper body. If an akhana is slain, any soul it contains is released automatically. An akhana can only hold one soul at a time. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"Akhanas bear charge over the duality of birth and death.\n\nThey perceive the existence of living things as crucial to maintaining cosmic balance. They also understand the profound inf luence living things have on the cosmos, and if left untended, its ability to create terrible consequences.\n\nIn this circumstance, life must give way to death.\n\nAkhanas wander the byways of the multiverse, constantly on the hunt for imbalances in life. How they judge these imbalances isn't well-understood by non-aeons, and the aeons are singularly unmotivated to justify akhanas' decisions when inquired about them. As a result, the focus of akhanas' attacks and attentions usually seems arbitrary or even random to most creatures-they don't always focus their attentions on the strongest or the weakest members of a group.\n\nAn akhana stands 5 ft. in height and weighs 120 pounds. Its strange central body seems vaporous, but is weirdly solid (and slimy) to the touch.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Animated Tank","cr":12,"xp":19200,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"construct","init":5,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":29,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":28,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +20 natural, -2 size","hp":144,"hd":"16d10+56","hdvalue":16,"fort":5,"ref":6,"will":5,"dr":"10/adamantine","immunities":["construct traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40}],"ranged":"3 Maxim M1910 machine guns +15 (2d8/19-20), Hotchkiss 6 pounder +15 (8d6/x3)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"integrated weaponry"},{"type":"telekinesis"},{"type":"vicious trample","details":"6d6+18, DC 30"}],"strength":35,"dexterity":12,"intelligence":13,"wisdom":10,"charisma":9,"baseatk":16,"cmb":30,"cmb_special":"+2 vs. bull rush","cmd":41,"cmd_special":"+2 vs. bull rush, can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Awesome Blow"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Point-Blank Shot"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Toughness"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Intimidate","value":15},{"skill":"Perception","value":26},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":20}],"languages":["Russian (can't speak)","telepathy 100 ft."],"sq":[{"type":"inexhaustible ammo"}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","troop (2-4)","squadron (5-12)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"Like a deranged caterpillar of grinding metal and protruding turrets, this massive armored vehicle dominates the battlefield, spitting hot lead and artillery-seemingly without a crew.","source":"AP 71","special_abilities":[{"type":"Inexhaustible Ammo","kind":"Su","details":"An animated tank loads and fires its weapons as a normal tank, but it telekinetically reloads from a supernaturally endless supply of ammunition."},{"type":"Integrated Weaponry","kind":"Ex","details":"An animated tank is equipped with three Maxim M1910 machine guns and two Hotchkiss 6 pounders built into its body. It treats these weapons as natural attacks and not manufactured weapons. It cannot make iterative attacks with these weapons. An animated tank has its weapons arranged on all sides of its body and can make three machine gun attacks and one Hotchkiss 6 pounder attack each round. An animated tank's weapons can still be targeted by effects that target manufactured weapons (such as magic weapon spells or sunder attempts), but cannot easily be harvested for use once the animated tank is destroyed. An animated tank is always proficient with its weapons, and its ranged weapons don't provoke attacks of opportunity when fired in melee combat."},{"type":"Telekinesis","kind":"Su","details":"The pickled brain that animates the tank possesses a supernatural ability to manipulate its surroundings and reload its armament. The animated tank can use telekinesis as a standard action every 1d4 rounds (caster level 16th)."},{"type":"Vicious Trample","kind":"Ex","details":"An animated tank's powerful metal treads deal 6d6+18 points of damage on a successful trample."}],"description":"The brains of great military commanders and tacticians need not go to waste simply because their mortal bodies have been slain. Preserved in glass vessels, bathed in nutrient fluids, and wired to strange energies and bizarre technologies, these organs are given new life, as their mental talents are preserved and tapped to independently control monstrous war machines. Though the methods, magic, and technology used differ between creators of these hulking engines, incarnations of these creatures typically take the form of captured siege engines and vehicles retrofitted to allow independent control by the pickled brains inside.\n\nAnimated tanks are perhaps the most dangerous of such animate siege engines. Thought haunted by some, and simply assumed by others to be well-commanded vehicles crewed by crack soldiers, these animated monstrosities are feared and loathed on battlefields across the front. Blessed with incredible armor and the ability to never tire or deplete their stocks of ammunition, these creatures run roughshod over trenches and barricades alike, grinding troops unfortunate enough to fall beneath their tracks to splinters of meat and bone. The tremendous range afforded by their armaments only makes matters worse for those forced to confront the lumbering monstrosities, and finding a weakness within their steel carcasses is nigh impossible.\n\nAnimated tanks are found in the company of one or more rifle or flamethrower troops; these soldiers are usually either keenly aware of the tank's unique magical animation, or wholly ignorant of its mysterious and taciturn movements as they simply follow their commander's orders without regard to the tank's missing crew. Those hearing the tanks' orders in their own heads, however, instantly realize that something isn't quite normal. As animated tanks are built with the armored frames of British Mark IV tanks-a common war wagon on First World War battlefields-few soldiers question the orders of their superiors when tasked with accompanying one of the beasts. Though Mark IV tanks could normally hold a crew of eight, the cabin of an animated tank is filled with strange technological and alchemical devices, allowing only four Medium creatures space to ride inside-that is, if the animated tank agrees to carry passengers.\n\nAnimated tanks were designed by Viktor Miloslav for use by the Russian Imperial Army, and it is thought that this mad experimentation and blasphemous use of the deceased is what triggered his exile to the cold wastes of Siberia and his imprisonment in the Akuvskaya prison camp. It is ultimately unknown how effective the creations of Viktor Miloslav proved on the battlefields of the Great War, or whether any of the monstrosities survived the war, as their shelled-out carcasses look little different from normal tanks, with the exception of a faint smell of formaldehyde and remnants of broken glass not usually found with tanks of this model. Whether some slumbering beast waits patiently in some forgotten barn or warehouse remains to be seen, or whether brave soldiers have laid this dangerous and blasphemous technology to rest is unknown, but hopefully Viktor Miloslav's mad designs have all been destroyed or lost forever.\n\nVariants\n\nViktor Miloslav is rumored to have created variations on the normal Mark V tank during his brief explorations into self-animated war machines during World War I.\n\n\"Female\" Animated Tank (CR 11): So named because it lacked the heavier Hotchkiss 6 pounder guns of its more robust counterpart, this variant makes up for its lack of explosive firepower with a bristling barrage of machine gun fire, being able to make up to five attacks per round with its Maxim M1910 machine guns. The tanks are otherwise identical in most respects, and few find a female animated tank's lack of Hotchkiss 6 pounder guns a relief when faced with its withering machine gun attacks.\n\nThe \"Moving Fortress\" (CR 13): Once word of Viktor Miloslav's inventions spread to Germany, the engineers there tried to replicate the effects he'd achieved, though it's unknown to what degree they succeeded. Should one of these specimens have survived, it would have been much more highly armored, built on the base of the German A7V tank-designed literally like a tracked, armored land ship. A moving fortress has 2 additional Hit Dice, and its natural armor bonus is increased by 5. Its single main gun, more robust than the Hotchkiss 6 pounder, deals an additional 4d6 points of damage, and the moving fortress is equipped with six Maxim M1910 machine guns.\n\nConstruction\n\nAn animated tank is built by retrofitting a preexisting tank and hard-wiring its pickled brain to the controls through strange technology, rather than crafting the construct's tank body from scratch. The secrets to preserving brains and connecting them to metal war wagons is lost, as is the nonmagical technological process by which Viktor Miloslav constructed the monstrosities found on Earth during the First World War. However, those able to inspect a destroyed specimen may be able to reconstruct the process. In addition to an animated tank's creation requirements-beyond the body of an intact tank-an animating brain must be harvested soon after its body is deceased, preserved with gentle repose, and subjected to a special nutrient bath before being revived and ultimately hooked into the tank. Only time and experimentation will reveal whether other secrets to this mysterious process were lost in the chaos of war on Earth.\n\nANIMATED TANK\n\nCL 12th; Price 200,000 gp\n\nCONSTRUCTION\n\nRequirements Craft Construct, animate object, geas/quest, resurrection, telekinesis; Skill Craft (blacksmithing), Knowledge (engineering), and Heal DC 25; Cost 100,000.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Aoandon","cr":12,"xp":19200,"alignment":"CE","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["incorporeal","native"],"init":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"true seeing"}],"ac":24,"ac_touch":24,"ac_flat_footed":16,"ac_mods":"+6 deflection, +7 Dex, +1 dodge","hp":152,"hd":"16d10+64","hdvalue":16,"fort":14,"ref":12,"will":12,"defensive_abilities":["incorporeal"],"speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":60,"maneuverability":"perfect"}],"melee":"touch of madness +19 touch (10d6)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","spell_like_abilities_caster_level":16,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":20,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"true seeing"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"darkness"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"mass pain strike"},{"spell":"waves of fatigue"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"bestow curse"},{"spell":"suffocation"}]}],"dexterity":24,"constitution":19,"intelligence":20,"wisdom":15,"charisma":22,"baseatk":16,"cmb":23,"cmd":40,"feats":[{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Mobility"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Fly)"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Intimidate)"},{"feat":"Spring Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Finesse"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (touch)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":22},{"skill":"Bluff","value":25},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":19},{"skill":"Fly","value":40},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":31},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":20},{"skill":"Knowledge (history)","value":10},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":10},{"skill":"Knowledge (nobility)","value":12},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":18},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":13},{"skill":"Perception","value":20},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":20},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":22},{"skill":"Stealth","value":22}],"languages":["Abyssal","Celestial","Common","Draconic","Giant","Infernal"],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This translucent, shaggy, horned monster shines with an eerie blue light, and its form trickles into vapor below the waist.","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 4","special_abilities":[{"type":"Touch of Madness","kind":"Su","details":"The touch of an aoandon causes maddening fear. As a standard action it can make an incorporeal touch attack that deals 10d6 damage. Any living creature damaged by an aoandon's touch attack must succeed at a DC 24 Will save or be confused for 1d4 rounds. A creature that succeeds at this saving throw can't be confused again by this aoandon's touch of madness for 10 minutes. This is a mind-affecting fear effect. The save DC is Charisma-based."}],"description":"An aoandon is an incorporeal outsider formed from the spirit of a woman who died pursuing some ill-fated relationship. An aoandon waits for her chance to seek revenge on those who wronged her in her mortal life. If that person is dead, she finds a surrogate-someone who reminds her of the wrongdoer-and acts out her delusions with unrelenting vindictiveness. These spirits can also appear as a result of mishaps with calling spells, but such instances are rare.\n\nCALLING AN AOANDON\n\nCalling an aoandon requires a paper lantern inscribed with runes and fueled by oils costing no less than 5,000 gp. Three or more creatures must chant the creature's name for 1 minute, then extinguish the lantern. There's a 1% chance per Hit Die the callers collectively possess that the aoandon is called. Relatives of the aoandon count as triple their normal Hit Dice. The aoandon isn't under the control of its conjurers, and can return to where she came from only after she has murdered at least one person she feels is responsible for her anguish.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Athach","cr":12,"xp":19200,"alignment":"CE","size":"Huge","type":"humanoid","subtypes":["giant"],"init":1,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":26,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":25,"ac_mods":"+2 armor, +1 Dex, +15 natural, -2 size","hp":161,"hd":"14d8+98","hdvalue":14,"fort":16,"ref":5,"will":7,"resists":[{"type":"cold","value":10}],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50}],"melee":"2 slams +19 (1d8+11), bite +19 (2d6+11 plus poison) or   heavy mace +19 (3d6+11), bite +17 (2d6+5 plus poison)","ranged":"rock +10 (2d6+16)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"rock throwing","details":"140 ft."},{"type":"swift claw"}],"strength":32,"dexterity":13,"constitution":25,"intelligence":7,"wisdom":12,"charisma":6,"baseatk":10,"cmb":23,"cmd":34,"feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Iron Will"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lunge"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":1,"special":"+9 jump"},{"skill":"Climb","value":20},{"skill":"Perception","value":12},{"skill":"Stealth","value":-7}],"languages":["Giant"],"environments":["cold hills","temperate hills"],"organizations":["solitary","gang (2-4)","tribe (7-12)"],"treasure":"standard (leather armor, heavy shield, heavy mace)","description_visual":"This giant's maw contains a pair of dripping tusks, but it is its gangly third arm that makes its appearance truly bizarre.","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 2","special_abilities":[{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Bite-injury; save Fort DC 24; frequency 1/round for 6 rounds; effect 1d4 Str; cure 2 consecutive saves."},{"type":"Swift Claw","kind":"Ex","details":"An athach can attack with its claw as a swift action, even when the creature's movement would normally restrict it to one attack. This attack is made at a +19 bonus and deals 1d10+11 points of damage, regardless of what other attacks are made on the athach's turn."}],"description":"An athach is a twisted kind of giant, cruel and thuggish. It lives to bring misery, ruin, and terror to weaker creatures. An individual may be nearly any human color, though its arms are often a darker color or even grayish. Its upper fangs are long, extending from its mouth like those of a ferocious beast, and it constantly drools a w Athachs thrive upon the fear of their victims, preferring to play with their prey for some time before indulging their vile and murderous natures. Tales tell of how athachs cut down orchards and ruin crops by night, leaving the ruins to be discovered by innocent villagers at the dawning of the following day. Further tales tell of how athachs desecrate graveyards by exhuming graves and scattering the bones of the dead about. The motivation behind these games seems to be sheer entertainment—some athachs are unusually creative in their antics, displaying ingenuity beyond their normal capacity, as if an athach in the throes of desecration and cruelty were prone to some form of divine inspiration.\n\nAn athach is 18 ft. tall and weighs 5,000 pounds. Athachs dislike other giants (and other monsters of their size) and either attack or flee from them, depending on whether the odds are in their favor. eakness-inducing poison. A group of athachs is usually a family unit, with gangs typically consisting of a group of siblings and full tribes consisting of parents and young.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""}];
